koldera-core uses or ships the third-party components below. They keep their own licences. This list names the
major components; each package's own licence text is in its distribution. Exact versions are pinned in
engine/pom.xml, renderer/pnpm-lock.yaml, scanner/pnpm-lock.yaml, server/Directory.Packages.props and docker/Dockerfile.

Linked into the PDF engine (Java)
  Apache PDFBox and xmpbox            Apache-2.0        https://pdfbox.apache.org/
  Jackson (databind, core)            Apache-2.0        https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson
  networknt json-schema-validator     Apache-2.0        https://github.com/networknt/json-schema-validator
  Apache Commons Logging              Apache-2.0        https://commons.apache.org/proper/commons-logging/
  Bouncy Castle (bcprov, bcpkix)      MIT-style (Bouncy Castle Licence)   https://www.bouncycastle.org/
  SLF4J (slf4j-nop)                   MIT               https://www.slf4j.org/

Run as separate processes (not linked into koldera-core)
  veraPDF                             GPL-3.0-or-later OR MPL-2.0 (dual licence)   https://verapdf.org/
      Started as a command-line process by the PDF engine; koldera-core does not link its libraries.
  Typst                               Apache-2.0        https://github.com/typst/typst
      Started as a command-line process by the document renderer.
  Chromium (headless shell)           BSD-3-Clause and the licences of its own dependencies   https://www.chromium.org/
      Started by Playwright for the HTML renderer and the web scanner.
  Squid (egress proxy container)      GPL-2.0-or-later  http://www.squid-cache.org/
      Shipped as a separate container image in docker/egress-proxy; not part of the koldera-core image.
  Caddy (front container)             Apache-2.0        https://caddyserver.com/
      Used as a separate container in docker/compose.yaml.
  oauth2-proxy (optional SSO)         MIT               https://github.com/oauth2-proxy/oauth2-proxy
      Used as a separate container in docker/compose.sso.yaml.

Node.js workers (renderer and scanner)
